# ── data/ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The JiveRepo root .gitignore has an unanchored `data/` pattern, which git
# applies at every directory level — it never descends into this directory
# at all as a result. Every level below must be explicitly re-included
# before a deeper pattern can take effect: git will not walk into an
# excluded directory to evaluate rules inside it, so a bare `!data/` alone
# is not sufficient. See docs/05-local-environment.md for the full note
# (relevant if this project is ever cloned into, or moved to, a different
# parent directory without this override).
#
# Directory levels are re-included explicitly, one at a time, rather than
# with a recursive `!data/raw/**` — a recursive negation placed before a
# recursive `data/raw/**` exclusion gets silently re-excluded by it, since
# `**` matches directories as well as files. Explicit per-level patterns
# avoid that trap entirely and stay easy to verify with `git check-ignore`.

!data/
!data/villains/
!data/villains/**

!data/raw/
!data/raw/*/
!data/raw/*/dt=*/
!data/raw/*/dt=*/hour=*/

# Generated landed Parquet: ignored by default...
data/raw/*/dt=*/hour=*/*
# ...except the committed sample partition (docs/05). Filename convention,
# not a `sample/` subdirectory — the sample must sit at a real dt=/hour=
# Hive path or DuckDB can't infer the partition columns, which would break
# `dbt run` on the very thing the sample exists to enable. `.md` placeholder
# in Phase 0, real `.parquet` in Phase 5. Phase 5 dbt sources must glob
# `*.parquet` explicitly so they never pick up this placeholder.
!data/raw/*/dt=*/hour=*/sample-*

data/quarantine/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ── dbt ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
transform/target/
transform/dbt_packages/
transform/logs/
transform/.user.yml

# ── Dagster ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `make dagster` points DAGSTER_HOME at orchestration/dagster_home/, which is
# where the instance writes real runtime state (run history sqlite DBs,
# compute logs, telemetry ID, the schedule/sensor tick store) once `dagster
# dev` actually runs. dagster.yaml itself (the committed config: concurrency
# pools, run coordinator) is the only file in that directory meant to be
# tracked.
orchestration/dagster_home/*
!orchestration/dagster_home/dagster.yaml

# ── Secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
api.txt
*.key
*.pem
credentials*
secrets*
*token*

#
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF-PROMPT.md
k8s-data-platform/HANDOFF.md
